/* Deep lessons — Asoslar va complexity (foundations).
 *
 * The section that decides whether everything after it works. A learner who
 * cannot look at n ≤ 200000 and say "so O(n²) is out" will spend the rest of
 * the roadmap writing correct solutions that time out.
 *
 * So nothing here is asserted without being derived: why halving gives log n,
 * why the doubling of a vector is amortised O(1), why comparison sorting
 * cannot beat n log n, and where the Master Theorem's three cases come from.
 * Every growth rate is shown as numbers a person can feel, not as a curve.
 *
 * Original text. Written for AlgoYo'l; nothing copied from any source.
 */

